{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UrT8xRtixEJPr6bv9RX48o","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Technical Design: Epic 7 Archive and Derived Views\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tThis document translates Epic 7 into an implementable design for canonical\n6\tprocess archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\n7\tIt is the implementation blueprint for preserving finalized low-level process\n8\thistory while keeping live process state, turns, and derived views separate from\n9\tcanonical truth.\n10\t\n11\t| Audience | Value |\n12\t|----------|-------|\n13\t| Reviewers | Validate that archive work follows the core platform architecture |\n14\t| Developers | Know which routes, services, Convex functions, contracts, and tests to build |\n15\t| Story Tech Sections | Reuse interfaces, flow designs, TC mappings, and chunk breakdowns |\n16\t\n17\tRelated documents:\n18\t\n19\t- Epic: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md`\n20\t- Test plan: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md`\n21\t- Architecture: `docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md`\n22\t- Epic 6 tech design: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md`\n23\t\n24\tOutput configuration: Config A. Epic 7 gets this `tech-design.md` and a separate\n25\t`test-plan.md`. The work crosses live process, Fastify, Convex, and client read\n26\tsurfaces, but the archive domain is coherent enough for one index document.\n27\t\n28\t## Spec Validation\n29\t\n30\tEpic 7 is implementation-ready. It is scoped to canonical finalized archive\n31\tentries, deterministic turn derivation, minimal structural derived views, and\n32\tbounded degraded reads. It explicitly avoids model-generated summaries,\n33\texternal-source attachment, and replacing the existing live WebSocket/upsert\n34\tmodel.\n35\t\n36\t| Issue | Spec Location | Resolution | Status |\n37\t|-------|---------------|------------|--------|\n38\t| Current `processHistoryItems` vocabulary differs from canonical archive taxonomy | Baseline, Tech Design Question 2 | Design adds new `archiveEntries` while bridging current history for compatibility. No historical migration/backfill is included. | Resolved - clarified |\n39\t| Finalization boundary must prevent raw deltas and interrupted partial objects | AC-2.x, Tech Design Question 3 | Design introduces `ArchiveFinalizationService` and `finalizationKey` idempotency. Only completed objects call append. | Resolved |\n40\t| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\n41\t| Minimal derived view could drift into summarization | AC-5.x | Design limits derived views to structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` records without generated summary body. | Resolved |\n42\t| Provenance links must not duplicate Epic 5/6 ownership logic | AC-6.x | Design stores nullable related ids and enriches through existing artifact/source services at read time. Archive entries remain visible when enrichment degrades. | Resolved |\n43\t\n44\tNo design-time deviation from the PRD or architecture is required. Fastify owns\n45\tarchive finalization policy, read orchestration, turn derivation, and derived\n46\tview refresh. Convex owns durable append/read storage, ordering, idempotency\n47\tguards, and optional cached projection records.\n48\t\n49\t## Tech Design Questions Answered\n50\t\n51\t| # | Epic Question | Design Answer |\n52\t|---|---------------|---------------|\n53\t| 1 | What durable schema stores archive entries, sequence numbers, related references, and idempotency keys? | Add `archiveEntries` with `projectId`, `processId`, `entryKind`, `sequence`, `finalizationKey`, `sourceObjectId`, body fields, related ids, status, and timestamps. Convex assigns sequence inside an append mutation and enforces `finalizationKey` idempotency per process. |\n54\t| 2 | What compatibility mapping bridges `processHistoryItems` and live updates, and is migration/backfill in scope? | Add compatibility helpers that map new finalized archive entries to existing process-history surfaces where needed. Existing `processHistoryItems` remain the legacy presentation read model. No historical migration/backfill is in scope for Epic 7. |\n55\t| 3 | What finalization boundary determines when entries are archived? | `ArchiveFinalizationService` is called only from completion points: accepted user responses, completed model/runtime objects, completed script emissions, finalized tool calls/results, and process events. Raw live deltas and interrupted partial objects never call append. |\n56\t| 4 | What derivation rules group archive entries into turns? | Turn derivation is deterministic over ordered archive entries. A `user_message` starts a new turn; following model/reasoning/script/tool/process entries attach to the active turn until the next `user_message`. Tool call/result correlation keeps paired tool entries in the same turn. |\n57\t| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\n58\t| 6 | What minimal derived-view representation should Epic 7 implement? | Implement structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` views with source turn/archive ids, optional labels, and status metadata. No model-generated summaries or summarization prompts. |\n59\t| 7 | How should source/artifact provenance link without duplicating ownership logic? | Archive entries store nullable related ids (`relatedArtifactVersionId`, `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, `relatedToolCallId`). Read services enrich from existing artifact/source services and degrade per entry when related records are unavailable. |\n60\t| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\n61\t| 9 | What idempotency strategy prevents duplicate archive entries? | `appendArchiveEntry` checks `processId + finalizationKey`. A replay returns the existing entry or no-ops. Sequence assignment happens only on first append. |\n62\t\n63\t## Context\n64\t\n65\tThe platform already has process history, but it is presentation history. The\n66\tcurrent `processHistoryItems` table supports the process work surface and live\n67\thistory upserts with a smaller vocabulary: `user_message`, `process_message`,\n68\t`progress_update`, `attention_request`, `side_work_update`, and\n69\t`process_event`. That is useful UI state, but it is not the full-fidelity\n70\tarchive the PRD requires for long-horizon context management.\n71\t\n72\tEpic 7 introduces canonical archive truth without tearing out the live surface.\n73\tFastify still normalizes runtime events into typed WebSocket upserts for active\n74\tUI state. Separately, completed process objects are finalized into archive\n75\tentries at low-level grain. This preserves the active interaction model while\n76\tmaking later turn/query/chunk work rebuildable from a stable durable record.\n77\t\n78\tThe design is deliberately conservative around derived views. Turns and\n79\tstructural views help later context-management work, but they do not replace\n80\tarchive entries. A derived turn or chunk candidate can be rebuilt from the\n81\tarchive. If derivation fails, the archive remains readable. That property is\n82\tmore important than early summarization convenience.\n83\t\n84\tEpic 7 also consumes Epic 5 and Epic 6 provenance without taking ownership of\n85\tthose domains. Artifact versions keep producing-process provenance in the\n86\tartifact/version model. Source provenance keeps repository identity in Epic 6\n87\trecords. Archive entries may link to those records and show related context, but\n88\tthey do not redefine artifact ownership or source attachment lifecycle.\n89\t\n90\t## System View\n91\t\n92\t### Top-Tier Surfaces\n93\t\n94\t| Surface | Source | This Epic's Role |\n95\t|---------|--------|------------------|\n96\t| Processes | Core architecture | Finalization points and archive read access live under one project/process |\n97\t| Archive | Core architecture | Primary Epic 7 domain; owns canonical entries and rebuildable projections |\n98\t| Projects | Core architecture | Project/process access gates archive reads |\n99\t| Artifacts | Core architecture | Provides related artifact-version context during archive reads |\n100\t| Sources | Core architecture + Epic 6 | Provides related source provenance context during archive reads |\n101\t| Client | Core architecture | Adds process-surface entry points for archive, turn, and structural-view reads |\n102\t\n103\t### Runtime Flow\n104\t\n105\t```mermaid\n106\tflowchart LR\n107\t    EXEC[Process/runtime completion points]\n108\t    FINAL[ArchiveFinalizationService]\n109\t    STORE[PlatformStore]\n110\t    X[(Convex Archive Tables)]\n111\t    READ[ArchiveReadService]\n112\t    DERIVE[TurnDerivationService]\n113\t    VIEWS[DerivedArchiveViewService]\n114\t    API[Fastify archive routes]\n115\t    UI[Client process/archive UI]\n116\t\n117\t    EXEC --> FINAL\n118\t    FINAL --> STORE\n119\t    STORE --> X\n120\t    UI --> API\n121\t    API --> READ\n122\t    READ --> STORE\n123\t    READ --> DERIVE\n124\t    DERIVE --> VIEWS\n125\t    VIEWS --> STORE\n126\t```\n127\t\n128\tThe append path is narrow and trusted. Fastify calls\n129\t`ArchiveFinalizationService` when a process object is complete. The service\n130\tnormalizes the finalized object into canonical archive entry shape and asks\n131\t`PlatformStore` to append it. Convex assigns sequence and enforces idempotency.\n132\t\n133\tThe read path is broader. Fastify routes call `ArchiveReadService` for archive\n134\tentries, `TurnDerivationService` for turns, and `DerivedArchiveViewService` for\n135\tstructural views. These services read durable archive data and enrich related\n136\tartifact/source context independently. A related-context failure degrades one\n137\tentry or view rather than hiding the archive.\n138\t\n139\t## Decisions\n140\t\n141\t| Decision | Rationale | Consequence |\n142\t|----------|-----------|-------------|\n143\t| Add new `archiveEntries` instead of replacing `processHistoryItems` | Current history is presentation-oriented and already used by live process surfaces | Epic 7 can preserve archive truth without destabilizing current UI |\n144\t| Fastify owns finalization policy | Architecture says Fastify owns orchestration and live-event normalization | Convex append functions are durable primitives with validators and idempotency guards |\n145\t| Convex assigns `sequence` atomically | Stable ordering must survive same timestamps and retries | Append mutation computes next sequence per process |\n146\t| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\n147\t| Turn references must stay stable across rebuilds | Derived views cannot dangle when turn cache is refreshed | Turns get deterministic `turnId` values and derived views store stable turn ids plus turn-index ranges, not Convex row ids |\n148\t| Derived views are structural only | Prevents scope creep into summarization | `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` contain boundaries/provenance, not generated summaries |\n149\t| No historical migration/backfill | Epic 7 is forward canonicalization plus compatibility bridge | Existing `processHistoryItems` remain visible, but old rows are not retroactively canonical |\n150\t\n151\t## Module Boundaries\n152\t\n153\t### File Architecture\n154\t\n155\t```\n156\tconvex/\n157\t├── archiveEntries.ts                         # NEW: append/read canonical archive entries\n158\t├── archiveTurns.ts                           # NEW: cached derived turn records\n159\t├── derivedArchiveViews.ts                    # NEW: structural derived-view records\n160\t└── schema.ts                                 # MODIFIED: archive tables and indexes\n161\t\n162\tapps/platform/shared/contracts/\n163\t├── archive.ts                                # NEW: archive/turn/derived-view contracts and route builders\n164\t├── process-work-surface.ts                   # MODIFIED: optional archive entry points/actions in process surface contract\n165\t└── index.ts                                  # MODIFIED: exports\n166\t\n167\tapps/platform/server/schemas/\n168\t└── archive.ts                                # NEW: Fastify route schemas for archive APIs\n169\t\n170\tapps/platform/server/routes/\n171\t└── archive.ts                                # NEW: authenticated archive/turn/derived-view routes\n172\t\n173\tapps/platform/server/services/archive/\n174\t├── archive-finalization.service.ts           # NEW: finalized-object to archive-entry mapping\n175\t├── archive-read.service.ts                   # NEW: archive read/enrichment/degraded-state orchestration\n176\t├── turn-derivation.service.ts                # NEW: deterministic turn derivation and rebuild\n177\t├── derived-archive-view.service.ts           # NEW: structural view creation/read/refresh\n178\t└── process-history-compat.service.ts         # NEW: bridge archive entries to existing history surface when needed\n179\t\n180\tapps/platform/server/services/projects/\n181\t└── platform-store.ts                         # MODIFIED: archive append/read/projection methods\n182\t\n183\tapps/platform/server/services/processes/\n184\t├── environment/process-environment.service.ts # MODIFIED: call finalization for execution/tool/process events\n185\t├── process-response.service.ts               # MODIFIED: archive accepted user responses\n186\t└── live/process-live-normalizer.ts           # UNCHANGED: live upserts remain current-object transport\n187\t\n188\tapps/platform/client/features/processes/\n189\t├── archive-section.ts                        # NEW: process archive read surface\n190\t├── archive-turns-section.ts                  # NEW: derived turn surface\n191\t└── derived-archive-views-section.ts          # NEW: structural derived-view surface\n192\t\n193\tapps/platform/client/app/\n194\t└── bootstrap.ts                              # MODIFIED: route archive actions to process/archive surfaces\n195\t\n196\ttests/\n197\t├── fixtures/archive.ts                       # NEW: archive/turn/view fixtures\n198\t├── service/server/archive-api.test.ts        # NEW: Fastify archive route tests\n199\t├── service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts # NEW: finalization and idempotency tests\n200\t├── service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts    # NEW: deterministic turn derivation tests\n201\t├── service/client/archive-section.test.ts    # NEW: client archive rendering tests\n202\t├── service/client/archive-turns-section.test.ts # NEW: turn surface rendering tests\n203\t└── service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts # NEW: derived-view UI tests\n204\t```\n205\t\n206\t### Module Responsibility Matrix\n207\t\n208\t| Module | Status | Responsibility | Dependencies | ACs Covered |\n209\t|--------|--------|----------------|--------------|-------------|\n210\t| `convex/archiveEntries.ts` | New | Append/read canonical entries, sequence assignment, idempotency guard, pagination | Convex schema | AC-1.x, AC-2.3, AC-3.x, AC-7.3 |\n211\t| `convex/archiveTurns.ts` | New | Store rebuildable cached turns | Convex schema | AC-4.x, AC-7.1 |\n212\t| `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts` | New | Store/read structural derived views | Convex schema | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\n213\t| `ArchiveFinalizationService` | New | Map completed process objects to archive entries; exclude deltas/partials | PlatformStore | AC-1.x, AC-2.x |\n214\t| `ArchiveReadService` | New | Read archive entries, enforce access via routes/services, enrich related context, degrade locally | PlatformStore, artifact/source services | AC-3.x, AC-6.x, AC-7.x |\n215\t| `TurnDerivationService` | New | Deterministically derive/rebuild turns from archive entries | PlatformStore | AC-4.x |\n216\t| `DerivedArchiveViewService` | New | Build/read non-summarizing structural views | PlatformStore, TurnDerivationService | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\n217\t| `ProcessHistoryCompatService` | New | Bridge archive entries to existing history surfaces without migration | ArchiveReadService | A7, Story 0 |\n218\t| `registerArchiveRoutes` | New | Fastify entry points, auth/access, request/response validation | ProcessAccessService, archive services | AC-3.x through AC-7.x |\n219\t| Client archive sections | New | Render archive, turns, structural views, empty/degraded states | Shared contracts/API client | AC-3.x, AC-4.x, AC-5.x, AC-6.x, AC-7.x |\n220\t\n221\t## Data Model\n222\t\n223\t### Convex `archiveEntries`\n224\t\n225\t```typescript\n226\texport const archiveEntryKindValidator = v.union(\n227\t  v.literal('user_message'),\n228\t  v.literal('model_message'),\n229\t  v.literal('reasoning'),\n230\t  v.literal('script_emission'),\n231\t  v.literal('tool_call'),\n232\t  v.literal('tool_result'),\n233\t  v.literal('process_event'),\n234\t);\n235\t\n236\texport const archiveEntriesTableFields = {\n237\t  projectId: v.string(),\n238\t  processId: v.id('processes'),\n239\t  entryKind: archiveEntryKindValidator,\n240\t  sequence: v.number(),\n241\t  lifecycleState: v.literal('finalized'),\n242\t  finalizationKey: v.string(),\n243\t  sourceObjectId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n244\t  bodyText: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n245\t  bodyData: v.union(\n246\t    v.object({\n247\t      jsonText: v.string(),\n248\t    }),\n249\t    v.null(),\n250\t  ),\n251\t  bodyFormat: v.union(v.literal('plain_text'), v.literal('markdown'), v.literal('structured'), v.literal('none')),\n252\t  relatedArtifactVersionId: v.union(v.id('artifactVersions'), v.null()),\n253\t  relatedSourceProvenanceId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n254\t  relatedToolCallId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n255\t  entryStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\n256\t  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n257\t  recordedAt: v.string(),\n258\t};\n259\t```\n260\t\n261\tIndexes:\n262\t\n263\t| Index | Fields | Purpose |\n264\t|-------|--------|---------|\n265\t| `by_processId_sequence` | `processId`, `sequence` | Canonical archive pagination |\n266\t| `by_processId_finalizationKey` | `processId`, `finalizationKey` | Idempotency guard |\n267\t| `by_projectId_processId_recordedAt` | `projectId`, `processId`, `recordedAt` | Project/process scoped diagnostics |\n268\t\n269\t`appendArchiveEntry` performs the final idempotency check and sequence assignment\n270\tinside one Convex mutation. Fastify can preflight finalization keys, but Convex\n271\towns the atomic guard.\n272\t\n273\t### Convex `archiveTurns`\n274\t\n275\t```typescript\n276\texport const archiveTurnsTableFields = {\n277\t  projectId: v.string(),\n278\t  processId: v.id('processes'),\n279\t  turnId: v.string(),\n280\t  turnIndex: v.number(),\n281\t  archiveEntryIds: v.array(v.id('archiveEntries')),\n282\t  startedAt: v.string(),\n283\t  endedAt: v.string(),\n284\t  turnStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\n285\t  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n286\t  rebuiltAt: v.string(),\n287\t};\n288\t```\n289\t\n290\tIndexes:\n291\t\n292\t| Index | Fields | Purpose |\n293\t|-------|--------|---------|\n294\t| `by_processId_turnId` | `processId`, `turnId` | Stable turn lookups across rebuilds |\n295\t| `by_processId_turnIndex` | `processId`, `turnIndex` | Turn pagination and stable ordering |\n296\t\n297\tTurns are cached because bounded reads matter for long processes. The cache is\n298\tnot canonical. `TurnDerivationService.rebuildTurns` must upsert turns by stable\n299\t`turnId` (`${processId}:turn:${turnIndex}`) so derived-view provenance stays\n300\tvalid across rebuilds.\n301\t\n302\t### Convex `derivedArchiveViews`\n303\t\n304\t```typescript\n305\texport const derivedArchiveViewsTableFields = {\n306\t  projectId: v.string(),\n307\t  processId: v.id('processes'),\n308\t  viewKind: v.union(v.literal('turn_range'), v.literal('chunk_candidate')),\n309\t  startTurnIndex: v.union(v.number(), v.null()),\n310\t  endTurnIndex: v.union(v.number(), v.null()),\n311\t  sourceTurnIds: v.array(v.string()),\n312\t  sourceArchiveEntryIds: v.array(v.id('archiveEntries')),\n313\t  title: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n314\t  bodyText: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n315\t  viewStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\n316\t  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n317\t  updatedAt: v.string(),\n318\t};\n319\t```\n320\t\n321\tIndexes:\n322\t\n323\t| Index | Fields | Purpose |\n324\t|-------|--------|---------|\n325\t| `by_processId_updatedAt` | `processId`, `updatedAt` | Derived-view reads |\n326\t\n327\tFor `turn_range`, `startTurnIndex` and `endTurnIndex` are required by Fastify\n328\tvalidation before persistence. For `chunk_candidate`, the view must include\n329\tsource turn ids and source archive entry ids; it must not include generated\n330\tsummary content. Derived-view rows may be deleted and recreated from turns; this\n331\tdoes not affect canonical archive entries.\n332\t\n333\tThe array fields in `archiveTurns` and `derivedArchiveViews` are intentionally\n334\tbounded. Epic 7 limits turn rows to one process turn and derived views to small\n335\tstructural groupings, not unbounded child lists. Long-process pagination stays\n336\tat the archive-entry and turn level rather than trying to persist one giant\n337\tderived record.\n338\t\n339\t## API Contracts\n340\t\n341\tShared contracts live in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts`.\n342\t\n343\t```typescript\n344\texport type ArchiveEntryKind =\n345\t  | 'user_message'\n346\t  | 'model_message'\n347\t  | 'reasoning'\n348\t  | 'script_emission'\n349\t  | 'tool_call'\n350\t  | 'tool_result'\n351\t  | 'process_event';\n352\t\n353\texport interface ArchiveEntry {\n354\t  archiveEntryId: string;\n355\t  projectId: string;\n356\t  processId: string;\n357\t  entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\n358\t  sequence: number;\n359\t  lifecycleState: 'finalized';\n360\t  finalizationKey: string;\n361\t  sourceObjectId: string | null;\n362\t  bodyText: string | null;\n363\t  bodyData: { jsonText: string } | null;\n364\t  bodyFormat: 'plain_text' | 'markdown' | 'structured' | 'none';\n365\t  relatedArtifactVersionId: string | null;\n366\t  relatedSourceProvenanceId: string | null;\n367\t  relatedToolCallId: string | null;\n368\t  entryStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n369\t  degradationReason: string | null;\n370\t  recordedAt: string;\n371\t}\n372\t\n373\texport interface ArchivePage {\n374\t  entries: ArchiveEntry[];\n375\t  page: { cursor: string | null; nextCursor: string | null; hasMore: boolean };\n376\t}\n377\t\n378\texport interface DerivedTurn {\n379\t  turnId: string;\n380\t  processId: string;\n381\t  turnIndex: number;\n382\t  archiveEntryIds: string[];\n383\t  startedAt: string;\n384\t  endedAt: string;\n385\t  turnStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n386\t  degradationReason: string | null;\n387\t}\n388\t\n389\texport interface DerivedArchiveView {\n390\t  derivedViewId: string;\n391\t  processId: string;\n392\t  viewKind: 'turn_range' | 'chunk_candidate';\n393\t  turnRange: { startIndex: number; endIndex: number } | null;\n394\t  sourceTurnIds: string[];\n395\t  sourceArchiveEntryIds: string[];\n396\t  title: string | null;\n397\t  bodyText: string | null;\n398\t  viewStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n399\t  degradationReason: string | null;\n400\t  updatedAt: string;\n401\t}\n402\t```\n403\t\n404\t### Routes\n405\t\n406\t| Operation | Method | Path | Service |\n407\t|-----------|--------|------|---------|\n408\t| Get process archive | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive` | `ArchiveReadService.getArchive` |\n409\t| Get process turns | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/turns` | `TurnDerivationService.getTurns` |\n410\t| Get derived archive views | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` |\n411\t| Refresh derived archive views | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views/refresh` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.refreshViews` |\n412\t\n413\tAll routes use existing actor resolution and `app.processAccessService` to\n414\tenforce project/process access before archive services run.\n415\t\n416\t### Route Validation and Error Responses\n417\t\n418\t`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts` should define these route schemas:\n419\t\n420\t- archive page query: `cursor?: string | null`, `limit?: number`\n421\t- turn page query: `cursor?: string | null`, `limit?: number`\n422\t- derived-view refresh body: empty object for Epic 7\n423\t\n424\tRoute responses:\n425\t\n426\t| Route | 200 | Errors |\n427\t|-------|-----|--------|\n428\t| `GET /archive` | `ArchivePage` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n429\t| `GET /archive/turns` | `{ turns, page }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n430\t| `GET /archive/derived-views` | `{ views }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n431\t| `POST /archive/derived-views/refresh` | `{ views, refreshStatus }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `409`, `422` |\n432\t\n433\tError codes:\n434\t\n435\t| Status | Code | Meaning |\n436\t|--------|------|---------|\n437\t| 401 | `UNAUTHENTICATED` | Actor is missing |\n438\t| 403 | `PROJECT_FORBIDDEN` | Actor lacks project access |\n439\t| 404 | `PROJECT_NOT_FOUND` | Project does not exist |\n440\t| 404 | `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` | Process does not exist in project |\n441\t| 409 | `ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT` | Derived-view refresh cannot safely reconcile with current archive state |\n442\t| 422 | `INVALID_ARCHIVE_REQUEST` | Cursor, limit, or derived-view refresh request is invalid |\n443\t\n444\t## Service Interfaces\n445\t\n446\t```typescript\n447\texport interface ArchiveFinalizationService {\n448\t  appendFinalizedEntry(args: {\n449\t    projectId: string;\n450\t    processId: string;\n451\t    entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\n452\t    finalizationKey: string;\n453\t    sourceObjectId?: string | null;\n454\t    bodyText?: string | null;\n455\t    bodyData?: { jsonText: string } | null;\n456\t    bodyFormat: ArchiveEntry['bodyFormat'];\n457\t    relatedArtifactVersionId?: string | null;\n458\t    relatedSourceProvenanceId?: string | null;\n459\t    relatedToolCallId?: string | null;\n460\t  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry>;\n461\t\n462\t  appendFromProcessHistoryItem(args: {\n463\t    projectId: string;\n464\t    processId: string;\n465\t    historyItem: ProcessHistoryItem;\n466\t  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry | null>;\n467\t}\n468\t\n469\texport interface ArchiveReadService {\n470\t  getArchive(args: {\n471\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n472\t    projectId: string;\n473\t    processId: string;\n474\t    cursor?: string | null;\n475\t    limit?: number;\n476\t  }): Promise<ArchivePage>;\n477\t}\n478\t\n479\texport interface TurnDerivationService {\n480\t  // Rebuilds cached turns by deterministic turnId rather than recreating\n481\t  // opaque row ids, so downstream view provenance remains stable.\n482\t  rebuildTurns(args: { projectId: string; processId: string }): Promise<DerivedTurn[]>;\n483\t  getTurns(args: {\n484\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n485\t    projectId: string;\n486\t    processId: string;\n487\t    cursor?: string | null;\n488\t    limit?: number;\n489\t  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\n490\t}\n491\t\n492\texport interface DerivedArchiveViewService {\n493\t  listViews(args: {\n494\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n495\t    projectId: string;\n496\t    processId: string;\n497\t  }): Promise<{ views: DerivedArchiveView[] }>;\n498\t\n499\t  refreshViews(args: {\n500\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n501\t    projectId: string;\n502\t    processId: string;\n503\t  }): Promise<{ views: DerivedArchiveView[]; refreshStatus: 'settled' | 'accepted' | 'degraded' }>;\n504\t}\n505\t```\n506\t\n507\t### PlatformStore Additions\n508\t\n509\t```typescript\n510\texport interface PlatformStore {\n511\t  appendArchiveEntry(args: {\n512\t    projectId: string;\n513\t    processId: string;\n514\t    entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\n515\t    finalizationKey: string;\n516\t    sourceObjectId?: string | null;\n517\t    bodyText?: string | null;\n518\t    bodyData?: { jsonText: string } | null;\n519\t    bodyFormat: ArchiveEntry['bodyFormat'];\n520\t    relatedArtifactVersionId?: string | null;\n521\t    relatedSourceProvenanceId?: string | null;\n522\t    relatedToolCallId?: string | null;\n523\t    entryStatus?: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n524\t    degradationReason?: string | null;\n525\t  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry>;\n526\t\n527\t  listArchiveEntries(args: {\n528\t    processId: string;\n529\t    cursor?: string | null;\n530\t    limit: number;\n531\t  }): Promise<ArchivePage>;\n532\t\n533\t  upsertArchiveTurns(args: {\n534\t    projectId: string;\n535\t    processId: string;\n536\t    turns: DerivedTurn[];\n537\t  }): Promise<void>;\n538\t\n539\t  listArchiveTurns(args: {\n540\t    processId: string;\n541\t    cursor?: string | null;\n542\t    limit: number;\n543\t  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\n544\t\n545\t  replaceDerivedArchiveViews(args: {\n546\t    projectId: string;\n547\t    processId: string;\n548\t    views: DerivedArchiveView[];\n549\t  }): Promise<void>;\n550\t\n551\t  listDerivedArchiveViews(args: {\n552\t    processId: string;\n553\t  }): Promise<DerivedArchiveView[]>;\n554\t}\n555\t```\n556\t\n557\tConvex function validators should mirror these shapes directly. Fastify\n558\tservices decide finalization, derivation, and refresh policy; `PlatformStore`\n559\texposes only durable append/read/upsert/replace operations.\n560\t\n561\t## Flow-by-Flow Design\n562\t\n563\t### Flow 1: Capture Finalized Archive Entries\n564\t\n565\tThis flow covers the Story 1 primitive boundary behind AC-1.1 through AC-1.4.\n566\tTrusted callers supply already-finalized archive-entry payloads to the durable\n567\tappend/read primitive. Convex owns the canonical row shape, taxonomy\n568\tvalidation, stable ordering, idempotency guard, related-id storage, and bounded\n569\tprimitive reads.\n570\t\n571\t```mermaid\n572\tsequenceDiagram\n573\t    participant P as Trusted Caller\n574\t    participant S as PlatformStore\n575\t    participant X as Convex archiveEntries\n576\t\n577\t    P->>S: appendArchiveEntry(write)\n578\t    Note over P,S: AC-1.1 finalized low-level entry payload\n579\t    S->>X: appendArchiveEntry mutation\n580\t    Note over S,X: AC-1.2/AC-1.3/AC-1.4 taxonomy, ordering, idempotency, related ids\n581\t    X-->>S: ArchiveEntry\n582\t    S-->>P: ArchiveEntry\n583\t```\n584\t\n585\t### Flow 2: Keep Live State Separate from Canonical Archive\n586\t\n587\tThis flow covers AC-2.1 through AC-2.3. Existing WebSocket upserts continue to\n588\tserve active UI state through `process-live-normalizer.ts` and\n589\t`process-live.ts`. Those live messages are not archive writes. Only completed\n590\tobjects that reach a finalization point call `ArchiveFinalizationService`,\n591\twhich maps finalized runtime/process objects into the Story 1 append primitive\n592\texactly once.\n593\t\n594\tRetries are safe because every finalized object supplies a `finalizationKey`.\n595\tExamples:\n596\t\n597\t- accepted user response: `response:${clientRequestId}`\n598\t- runtime model message: `model:${sourceObjectId}`\n599\t- tool call/result pair: `tool:${relatedToolCallId}:call` and `tool:${relatedToolCallId}:result`\n600\t- process event: `event:${sourceObjectId}`\n601\t\n602\t### Flow 3: Read and Reopen Archive\n603\t\n604\tThis flow covers AC-3.1 through AC-3.4. The user reads archive entries through\n605\tFastify routes under the existing process path. Archive reads do not depend on\n606\tenvironment state or live WebSocket state. `ArchiveReadService` fetches one\n607\tbounded page from Convex, applies route validation and access rules, and\n608\treturns archive response rows for the client surface to render.\n609\t\n610\tThis flow owns displaying degraded entries already present in the response\n611\tcontract. Deep artifact/source enrichment and lookup-failure degradation\n612\tsemantics are added in Flow 6. Read-time degradation must not mutate the\n613\tcanonical `archiveEntries` row unless the row itself was originally persisted\n614\tas degraded.\n615\t\n616\t### Flow 4: Derive Turns\n617\t\n618\tThis flow covers AC-4.1 through AC-4.4. Turn derivation reads archive entries\n619\tin ascending `sequence`, groups them deterministically, and writes cached turns\n620\twhen refresh/rebuild is requested.\n621\t\n622\tGrouping rules:\n623\t\n624\t1. `user_message` starts a new turn.\n625\t2. Entries before the first user message form turn `0` if they exist.\n626\t3. `model_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`,\n627\t   `tool_result`, and `process_event` attach to the active turn.\n628\t  4. A `tool_result` with `relatedToolCallId` stays in the same turn as its\n629\t   matching `tool_call` when both are present.\n630\t  5. Degraded related context degrades the turn, not the archive entries.\n631\t\n632\tRebuild behavior is explicit: Epic 7 rebuilds turns on turn/derived-view read\n633\tor explicit derived-view refresh, not on every archive append. Rebuild upserts by\n634\tstable `turnId` and `turnIndex`.\n635\t\n636\t### Flow 5: Produce Minimal Structural Views\n637\t\n638\tThis flow covers AC-5.1 through AC-5.5. Structural views are generated from\n639\tturns, not from raw live state. The first slice produces:\n640\t\n641\t- `turn_range`: one contiguous range of turn indexes with source entry ids\n642\t- `chunk_candidate`: a candidate grouping over one or more turns for future\n643\t  context-management work\n644\t\n645\tNeither view contains model-generated summaries. `bodyText`, when present, is a\n646\tdeterministic label or structural note such as `Turns 4-8`.\n647\t\n648\t### Flow 6: Connect Provenance\n649\t\n650\tThis flow covers AC-6.1 through AC-6.3. Archive entries store nullable related\n651\tids. Building on the Flow 3 archive read surface, read services enrich when\n652\tpossible:\n653\t\n654\t- artifact context through `PlatformStore.listArtifactVersions` or a targeted\n655\t  artifact-version read helper\n656\t- source context through Epic 6 `sourceProvenance` reads\n657\t- tool context through `relatedToolCallId`\n658\t\n659\tIf a related record is unavailable, the entry remains visible. This flow owns\n660\tthe artifact/source lookup-failure degradation semantics: the archive entry\n661\tstatus becomes `degraded` for the read response, or an enriched response\n662\tincludes degraded related-context metadata without mutating the stored\n663\tcanonical entry. Story 3 remains responsible for rendering that response\n664\tstate to the user.\n665\t\n666\t### Flow 7: Return Later and Bound Long Reads\n667\t\n668\tThis flow covers AC-7.1 through AC-7.3. Archive entries, turns, and derived\n669\tviews are durable or rebuildable from durable entries. Reads use cursor\n670\tpagination with default limits:\n671\t\n672\t- archive entries: default 100, max 200\n673\t- turns: default 50, max 100\n674\t- derived views: default 50\n675\t\n676\tA derived-view read or rebuild failure does not block archive reads. Routes\n677\treturn degraded view state for derived failures and keep archive entries\n678\tavailable.\n679\t\n680\t## Implementation Chunks\n681\t\n682\t| Chunk | Story | Scope | ACs | Primary Tests |\n683\t|-------|-------|-------|-----|---------------|\n684\t| 0 | Foundation | Contracts, Convex schema, fixtures, error codes, compatibility mapping skeletons | All support | Relevant sections: API Contracts, Data Model. Non-TC: archive contract vocabulary and finalized-only schema test |\n685\t| 1 | Archive persistence | Append/read entries, taxonomy, ordering, idempotency, related ids | AC-1.x | Relevant sections: Flow 1, Data Model. Non-TC: atomic sequence assignment and primitive idempotency |\n686\t| 2 | Finalization boundary | Completion hooks, live/archive separation, retry idempotency | AC-2.x | Relevant sections: Flow 2, Service Interfaces. Non-TC: live-history separation, compatibility mapping decision |\n687\t| 3 | Archive read/reopen | Routes, access controls, empty state, bounded page contract, environment-loss reads, degraded-entry display | AC-3.x | Relevant sections: Flow 3, Route Validation. Non-TC: invalid archive request handling |\n688\t| 4 | Turn derivation | Deterministic grouping, cached rebuild, degraded turns | AC-4.x | Relevant sections: Flow 4, Data Model. Non-TC: turn-zero grouping, rebuild stability |\n689\t| 5 | Structural derived views | `turn_range`, `chunk_candidate`, refresh, degradation | AC-5.x | Relevant sections: Flow 5, Route Validation. Non-TC: no generated summary body, stale/rebuilt derived views |\n690\t| 6 | Provenance coherence | Artifact/source enrichment and related-record lookup degradation semantics | AC-6.x | Relevant sections: Flow 6, API Contracts. Non-TC: none |\n691\t| 7 | Reopen/bounded reads | Reload behavior, derived failures, long-process pagination hardening | AC-7.x | Relevant sections: Flow 7, Route Validation. Non-TC: none |\n692\t\n693\t## Verification\n694\t\n695\t| Script | Command | Use |\n696\t|--------|---------|-----|\n697\t| `red-verify` | `pnpm run red-verify` | After skeleton and Red tests |\n698\t| `verify` | `pnpm run verify` | Standard development gate |\n699\t| `green-verify` | `pnpm run green-verify` | After implementation passes tests |\n700\t| `verify-all` | `pnpm run verify-all` | Story/Epic completion |\n701\t\n702\t## Deferred Items\n703\t\n704\t| Item | Related AC | Reason Deferred | Future Work |\n705\t|------|------------|-----------------|-------------|\n706\t| Historical migration/backfill from `processHistoryItems` | A7 | Epic 7 starts forward canonical archive and compatibility bridge | Later migration if needed |\n707\t| Model-generated summaries | Scope, AC-5.x | Structural views only | Later context-management epic |\n708\t| Model-specific prompt packing | Scope | Not required for archive truth | Later context-management epic |\n709\t| External-source archive integration | Scope | Epic 6/7 sequence is repository-focused | Later source-integration work |\n710\t\n711\t## Resolved Implementation Decisions\n712\t\n713\t| Decision | Applied In |\n714\t|----------|------------|\n715\t| `relatedSourceProvenanceId` is implemented as the stable Epic 6 provenance identifier and stays string-shaped in shared contracts unless cross-table typing becomes frictionless. | Chunk 6 |\n716\t| Turn cache rebuild happens on turn/derived-view read or explicit refresh, not on every archive append. | Chunk 4 |\n717\t| Compatibility mapping does not publish archive entries back into the live history stream. Live history publisher remains unchanged. | Chunk 2 |\n718\t\n719\t## Self-Review Checklist\n720\t\n721\t- [x] Every Epic 7 AC has a module owner.\n722\t- [x] Every Epic 7 Tech Design Question is answered.\n723\t- [x] Canonical archive and live upserts stay separate.\n724\t- [x] Turns and derived views are rebuildable, not canonical.\n725\t- [x] Structural views exclude generated summaries.\n726\t- [x] Verification commands use project scripts.\n727\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9eda3ca-6602-4708-99a5-3d7fcbb61de5","uuid":"e61146bd-1e53-4337-a2a4-cbc6b423e37f","timestamp":"2026-05-05T18:51:50.368Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md","content":"# Technical Design: Epic 7 Archive and Derived Views\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis document translates Epic 7 into an implementable design for canonical\nprocess archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\nIt is the implementation blueprint for preserving finalized low-level process\nhistory while keeping live process state, turns, and derived views separate from\ncanonical truth.\n\n| Audience | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| Reviewers | Validate that archive work follows the core platform architecture |\n| Developers | Know which routes, services, Convex functions, contracts, and tests to build |\n| Story Tech Sections | Reuse interfaces, flow designs, TC mappings, and chunk breakdowns |\n\nRelated documents:\n\n- Epic: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md`\n- Test plan: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md`\n- Architecture: `docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md`\n- Epic 6 tech design: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md`\n\nOutput configuration: Config A. Epic 7 gets this `tech-design.md` and a separate\n`test-plan.md`. The work crosses live process, Fastify, Convex, and client read\nsurfaces, but the archive domain is coherent enough for one index document.\n\n## Spec Validation\n\nEpic 7 is implementation-ready. It is scoped to canonical finalized archive\nentries, deterministic turn derivation, minimal structural derived views, and\nbounded degraded reads. It explicitly avoids model-generated summaries,\nexternal-source attachment, and replacing the existing live WebSocket/upsert\nmodel.\n\n| Issue | Spec Location | Resolution | Status |\n|-------|---------------|------------|--------|\n| Current `processHistoryItems` vocabulary differs from canonical archive taxonomy | Baseline, Tech Design Question 2 | Design adds new `archiveEntries` while bridging current history for compatibility. No historical migration/backfill is included. | Resolved - clarified |\n| Finalization boundary must prevent raw deltas and interrupted partial objects | AC-2.x, Tech Design Question 3 | Design introduces `ArchiveFinalizationService` and `finalizationKey` idempotency. Only completed objects call append. | Resolved |\n| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\n| Minimal derived view could drift into summarization | AC-5.x | Design limits derived views to structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` records without generated summary body. | Resolved |\n| Provenance links must not duplicate Epic 5/6 ownership logic | AC-6.x | Design stores nullable related ids and enriches through existing artifact/source services at read time. Archive entries remain visible when enrichment degrades. | Resolved |\n\nNo design-time deviation from the PRD or architecture is required. Fastify owns\narchive finalization policy, read orchestration, turn derivation, and derived\nview refresh. Convex owns durable append/read storage, ordering, idempotency\nguards, and optional cached projection records.\n\n## Tech Design Questions Answered\n\n| # | Epic Question | Design Answer |\n|---|---------------|---------------|\n| 1 | What durable schema stores archive entries, sequence numbers, related references, and idempotency keys? | Add `archiveEntries` with `projectId`, `processId`, `entryKind`, `sequence`, `finalizationKey`, `sourceObjectId`, body fields, related ids, status, and timestamps. Convex assigns sequence inside an append mutation and enforces `finalizationKey` idempotency per process. |\n| 2 | What compatibility mapping bridges `processHistoryItems` and live updates, and is migration/backfill in scope? | Add compatibility helpers that map new finalized archive entries to existing process-history surfaces where needed. Existing `processHistoryItems` remain the legacy presentation read model. No historical migration/backfill is in scope for Epic 7. |\n| 3 | What finalization boundary determines when entries are archived? | `ArchiveFinalizationService` is called only from completion points: accepted user responses, completed model/runtime objects, completed script emissions, finalized tool calls/results, and process events. Raw live deltas and interrupted partial objects never call append. |\n| 4 | What derivation rules group archive entries into turns? | Turn derivation is deterministic over ordered archive entries. A `user_message` starts a new turn; following model/reasoning/script/tool/process entries attach to the active turn until the next `user_message`. Tool call/result correlation keeps paired tool entries in the same turn. |\n| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\n| 6 | What minimal derived-view representation should Epic 7 implement? | Implement structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` views with source turn/archive ids, optional labels, and status metadata. No model-generated summaries or summarization prompts. |\n| 7 | How should source/artifact provenance link without duplicating ownership logic? | Archive entries store nullable related ids (`relatedArtifactVersionId`, `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, `relatedToolCallId`). Read services enrich from existing artifact/source services and degrade per entry when related records are unavailable. |\n| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\n| 9 | What idempotency strategy prevents duplicate archive entries? | `appendArchiveEntry` checks `processId + finalizationKey`. A replay returns the existing entry or no-ops. Sequence assignment happens only on first append. |\n\n## Context\n\nThe platform already has process history, but it is presentation history. The\ncurrent `processHistoryItems` table supports the process work surface and live\nhistory upserts with a smaller vocabulary: `user_message`, `process_message`,\n`progress_update`, `attention_request`, `side_work_update`, and\n`process_event`. That is useful UI state, but it is not the full-fidelity\narchive the PRD requires for long-horizon context management.\n\nEpic 7 introduces canonical archive truth without tearing out the live surface.\nFastify still normalizes runtime events into typed WebSocket upserts for active\nUI state. Separately, completed process objects are finalized into archive\nentries at low-level grain. This preserves the active interaction model while\nmaking later turn/query/chunk work rebuildable from a stable durable record.\n\nThe design is deliberately conservative around derived views. Turns and\nstructural views help later context-management work, but they do not replace\narchive entries. A derived turn or chunk candidate can be rebuilt from the\narchive. If derivation fails, the archive remains readable. That property is\nmore important than early summarization convenience.\n\nEpic 7 also consumes Epic 5 and Epic 6 provenance without taking ownership of\nthose domains. Artifact versions keep producing-process provenance in the\nartifact/version model. Source provenance keeps repository identity in Epic 6\nrecords. Archive entries may link to those records and show related context, but\nthey do not redefine artifact ownership or source attachment lifecycle.\n\n## System View\n\n### Top-Tier Surfaces\n\n| Surface | Source | This Epic's Role |\n|---------|--------|------------------|\n| Processes | Core architecture | Finalization points and archive read access live under one project/process |\n| Archive | Core architecture | Primary Epic 7 domain; owns canonical entries and rebuildable projections |\n| Projects | Core architecture | Project/process access gates archive reads |\n| Artifacts | Core architecture | Provides related artifact-version context during archive reads |\n| Sources | Core architecture + Epic 6 | Provides related source provenance context during archive reads |\n| Client | Core architecture | Adds process-surface entry points for archive, turn, and structural-view reads |\n\n### Runtime Flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    EXEC[Process/runtime completion points]\n    FINAL[ArchiveFinalizationService]\n    STORE[PlatformStore]\n    X[(Convex Archive Tables)]\n    READ[ArchiveReadService]\n    DERIVE[TurnDerivationService]\n    VIEWS[DerivedArchiveViewService]\n    API[Fastify archive routes]\n    UI[Client process/archive UI]\n\n    EXEC --> FINAL\n    FINAL --> STORE\n    STORE --> X\n    UI --> API\n    API --> READ\n    READ --> STORE\n    READ --> DERIVE\n    DERIVE --> VIEWS\n    VIEWS --> STORE\n```\n\nThe append path is narrow and trusted. Fastify calls\n`ArchiveFinalizationService` when a process object is complete. The service\nnormalizes the finalized object into canonical archive entry shape and asks\n`PlatformStore` to append it. Convex assigns sequence and enforces idempotency.\n\nThe read path is broader. Fastify routes call `ArchiveReadService` for archive\nentries, `TurnDerivationService` for turns, and `DerivedArchiveViewService` for\nstructural views. These services read durable archive data and enrich related\nartifact/source context independently. A related-context failure degrades one\nentry or view rather than hiding the archive.\n\n## Decisions\n\n| Decision | Rationale | Consequence |\n|----------|-----------|-------------|\n| Add new `archiveEntries` instead of replacing `processHistoryItems` | Current history is presentation-oriented and already used by live process surfaces | Epic 7 can preserve archive truth without destabilizing current UI |\n| Fastify owns finalization policy | Architecture says Fastify owns orchestration and live-event normalization | Convex append functions are durable primitives with validators and idempotency guards |\n| Convex assigns `sequence` atomically | Stable ordering must survive same timestamps and retries | Append mutation computes next sequence per process |\n| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\n| Turn references must stay stable across rebuilds | Derived views cannot dangle when turn cache is refreshed | Turns get deterministic `turnId` values and derived views store stable turn ids plus turn-index ranges, not Convex row ids |\n| Derived views are structural only | Prevents scope creep into summarization | `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` contain boundaries/provenance, not generated summaries |\n| No historical migration/backfill | Epic 7 is forward canonicalization plus compatibility bridge | Existing `processHistoryItems` remain visible, but old rows are not retroactively canonical |\n\n## Module Boundaries\n\n### File Architecture\n\n```\nconvex/\n├── archiveEntries.ts                         # NEW: append/read canonical archive entries\n├── archiveTurns.ts                           # NEW: cached derived turn records\n├── derivedArchiveViews.ts                    # NEW: structural derived-view records\n└── schema.ts                                 # MODIFIED: archive tables and indexes\n\napps/platform/shared/contracts/\n├── archive.ts                                # NEW: archive/turn/derived-view contracts and route builders\n├── process-work-surface.ts                   # MODIFIED: optional archive entry points/actions in process surface contract\n└── index.ts                                  # MODIFIED: exports\n\napps/platform/server/schemas/\n└── archive.ts                                # NEW: Fastify route schemas for archive APIs\n\napps/platform/server/routes/\n└── archive.ts                                # NEW: authenticated archive/turn/derived-view routes\n\napps/platform/server/services/archive/\n├── archive-finalization.service.ts           # NEW: finalized-object to archive-entry mapping\n├── archive-read.service.ts                   # NEW: archive read/enrichment/degraded-state orchestration\n├── turn-derivation.service.ts                # NEW: deterministic turn derivation and rebuild\n├── derived-archive-view.service.ts           # NEW: structural view creation/read/refresh\n└── process-history-compat.service.ts         # NEW: bridge archive entries to existing history surface when needed\n\napps/platform/server/services/projects/\n└── platform-store.ts                         # MODIFIED: archive append/read/projection methods\n\napps/platform/server/services/processes/\n├── environment/process-environment.service.ts # MODIFIED: call finalization for execution/tool/process events\n├── process-response.service.ts               # MODIFIED: archive accepted user responses\n└── live/process-live-normalizer.ts           # UNCHANGED: live upserts remain current-object transport\n\napps/platform/client/features/processes/\n├── archive-section.ts                        # NEW: process archive read surface\n├── archive-turns-section.ts                  # NEW: derived turn surface\n└── derived-archive-views-section.ts          # NEW: structural derived-view surface\n\napps/platform/client/app/\n└── bootstrap.ts                              # MODIFIED: route archive actions to process/archive surfaces\n\ntests/\n├── fixtures/archive.ts                       # NEW: archive/turn/view fixtures\n├── service/server/archive-api.test.ts        # NEW: Fastify archive route tests\n├── service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts # NEW: finalization and idempotency tests\n├── service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts    # NEW: deterministic turn derivation tests\n├── service/client/archive-section.test.ts    # NEW: client archive rendering tests\n├── service/client/archive-turns-section.test.ts # NEW: turn surface rendering tests\n└── service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts # NEW: derived-view UI tests\n```\n\n### Module Responsibility Matrix\n\n| Module | Status | Responsibility | Dependencies | ACs Covered |\n|--------|--------|----------------|--------------|-------------|\n| `convex/archiveEntries.ts` | New | Append/read canonical entries, sequence assignment, idempotency guard, pagination | Convex schema | AC-1.x, AC-2.3, AC-3.x, AC-7.3 |\n| `convex/archiveTurns.ts` | New | Store rebuildable cached turns | Convex schema | AC-4.x, AC-7.1 |\n| `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts` | New | Store/read structural derived views | Convex schema | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\n| `ArchiveFinalizationService` | New | Map completed process objects to archive entries; exclude deltas/partials | PlatformStore | AC-1.x, AC-2.x |\n| `ArchiveReadService` | New | Read archive entries, enforce access via routes/services, enrich related context, degrade locally | PlatformStore, artifact/source services | AC-3.x, AC-6.x, AC-7.x |\n| `TurnDerivationService` | New | Deterministically derive/rebuild turns from archive entries | PlatformStore | AC-4.x |\n| `DerivedArchiveViewService` | New | Build/read non-summarizing structural views | PlatformStore, TurnDerivationService | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\n| `ProcessHistoryCompatService` | New | Bridge archive entries to existing history surfaces without migration | ArchiveReadService | A7, Story 0 |\n| `registerArchiveRoutes` | New | Fastify entry points, auth/access, request/response validation | ProcessAccessService, archive services | AC-3.x through AC-7.x |\n| Client archive sections | New | Render archive, turns, structural views, empty/degraded states | Shared contracts/API client | AC-3.x, AC-4.x, AC-5.x, AC-6.x, AC-7.x |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Convex `archiveEntries`\n\n```typescript\nexport const archiveEntryKindValidator = v.union(\n  v.literal('user_message'),\n  v.literal('model_message'),\n  v.literal('reasoning'),\n  v.literal('script_emission'),\n  v.literal('tool_call'),\n  v.literal('tool_result'),\n  v.literal('process_event'),\n);\n\nexport const archiveEntriesTableFields = {\n  projectId: v.string(),\n  processId: v.id('processes'),\n  entryKind: archiveEntryKindValidator,\n  sequence: v.number(),\n  lifecycleState: v.literal('finalized'),\n  finalizationKey: v.string(),\n  sourceObjectId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n  bodyText: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n  bodyData: v.union(\n    v.object({\n      jsonText: v.string(),\n    }),\n    v.null(),\n  ),\n  bodyFormat: v.union(v.literal('plain_text'), v.literal('markdown'), v.literal('structured'), v.literal('none')),\n  relatedArtifactVersionId: v.union(v.id('artifactVersions'), v.null()),\n  relatedSourceProvenanceId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n  relatedToolCallId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n  entryStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\n  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n  recordedAt: v.string(),\n};\n```\n\nIndexes:\n\n| Index | Fields | Purpose |\n|-------|--------|---------|\n| `by_processId_sequence` | `processId`, `sequence` | Canonical archive pagination |\n| `by_processId_finalizationKey` | `processId`, `finalizationKey` | Idempotency guard |\n| `by_projectId_processId_recordedAt` | `projectId`, `processId`, `recordedAt` | Project/process scoped diagnostics |\n\n`appendArchiveEntry` performs the final idempotency check and sequence assignment\ninside one Convex mutation. Fastify can preflight finalization keys, but Convex\nowns the atomic guard.\n\n### Convex `archiveTurns`\n\n```typescript\nexport const archiveTurnsTableFields = {\n  projectId: v.string(),\n  processId: v.id('processes'),\n  turnId: v.string(),\n  turnIndex: v.number(),\n  archiveEntryIds: v.array(v.id('archiveEntries')),\n  startedAt: v.string(),\n  endedAt: v.string(),\n  turnStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\n  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n  rebuiltAt: v.string(),\n};\n```\n\nIndexes:\n\n| Index | Fields | Purpose |\n|-------|--------|---------|\n| `by_processId_turnId` | `processId`, `turnId` | Stable turn lookups across rebuilds |\n| `by_processId_turnIndex` | `processId`, `turnIndex` | Turn pagination and stable ordering |\n\nTurns are cached because bounded reads matter for long processes. The cache is\nnot canonical. `TurnDerivationService.rebuildTurns` must upsert turns by stable\n`turnId` (`${processId}:turn:${turnIndex}`) so derived-view provenance stays\nvalid across rebuilds.\n\n### Convex `derivedArchiveViews`\n\n```typescript\nexport const derivedArchiveViewsTableFields = {\n  projectId: v.string(),\n  processId: v.id('processes'),\n  viewKind: v.union(v.literal('turn_range'), v.literal('chunk_candidate')),\n  startTurnIndex: v.union(v.number(), v.null()),\n  endTurnIndex: v.union(v.number(), v.null()),\n  sourceTurnIds: v.array(v.string()),\n  sourceArchiveEntryIds: v.array(v.id('archiveEntries')),\n  title: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n  bodyText: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n  viewStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\n  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n  updatedAt: v.string(),\n};\n```\n\nIndexes:\n\n| Index | Fields | Purpose |\n|-------|--------|---------|\n| `by_processId_updatedAt` | `processId`, `updatedAt` | Derived-view reads |\n\nFor `turn_range`, `startTurnIndex` and `endTurnIndex` are required by Fastify\nvalidation before persistence. For `chunk_candidate`, the view must include\nsource turn ids and source archive entry ids; it must not include generated\nsummary content. Derived-view rows may be deleted and recreated from turns; this\ndoes not affect canonical archive entries.\n\nThe array fields in `archiveTurns` and `derivedArchiveViews` are intentionally\nbounded. Epic 7 limits turn rows to one process turn and derived views to small\nstructural groupings, not unbounded child lists. Long-process pagination stays\nat the archive-entry and turn level rather than trying to persist one giant\nderived record.\n\n## API Contracts\n\nShared contracts live in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts`.\n\n```typescript\nexport type ArchiveEntryKind =\n  | 'user_message'\n  | 'model_message'\n  | 'reasoning'\n  | 'script_emission'\n  | 'tool_call'\n  | 'tool_result'\n  | 'process_event';\n\nexport interface ArchiveEntry {\n  archiveEntryId: string;\n  projectId: string;\n  processId: string;\n  entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\n  sequence: number;\n  lifecycleState: 'finalized';\n  finalizationKey: string;\n  sourceObjectId: string | null;\n  bodyText: string | null;\n  bodyData: { jsonText: string } | null;\n  bodyFormat: 'plain_text' | 'markdown' | 'structured' | 'none';\n  relatedArtifactVersionId: string | null;\n  relatedSourceProvenanceId: string | null;\n  relatedToolCallId: string | null;\n  entryStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n  degradationReason: string | null;\n  recordedAt: string;\n}\n\nexport interface ArchivePage {\n  entries: ArchiveEntry[];\n  page: { cursor: string | null; nextCursor: string | null; hasMore: boolean };\n}\n\nexport interface DerivedTurn {\n  turnId: string;\n  processId: string;\n  turnIndex: number;\n  archiveEntryIds: string[];\n  startedAt: string;\n  endedAt: string;\n  turnStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n  degradationReason: string | null;\n}\n\nexport interface DerivedArchiveView {\n  derivedViewId: string;\n  processId: string;\n  viewKind: 'turn_range' | 'chunk_candidate';\n  turnRange: { startIndex: number; endIndex: number } | null;\n  sourceTurnIds: string[];\n  sourceArchiveEntryIds: string[];\n  title: string | null;\n  bodyText: string | null;\n  viewStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n  degradationReason: string | null;\n  updatedAt: string;\n}\n```\n\n### Routes\n\n| Operation | Method | Path | Service |\n|-----------|--------|------|---------|\n| Get process archive | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive` | `ArchiveReadService.getArchive` |\n| Get process turns | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/turns` | `TurnDerivationService.getTurns` |\n| Get derived archive views | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` |\n| Refresh derived archive views | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views/refresh` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.refreshViews` |\n\nAll routes use existing actor resolution and `app.processAccessService` to\nenforce project/process access before archive services run.\n\n### Route Validation and Error Responses\n\n`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts` should define these route schemas:\n\n- archive page query: `cursor?: string | null`, `limit?: number`\n- turn page query: `cursor?: string | null`, `limit?: number`\n- derived-view refresh body: empty object for Epic 7\n\nRoute responses:\n\n| Route | 200 | Errors |\n|-------|-----|--------|\n| `GET /archive` | `ArchivePage` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n| `GET /archive/turns` | `{ turns, page }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n| `GET /archive/derived-views` | `{ views }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n| `POST /archive/derived-views/refresh` | `{ views, refreshStatus }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `409`, `422` |\n\nError codes:\n\n| Status | Code | Meaning |\n|--------|------|---------|\n| 401 | `UNAUTHENTICATED` | Actor is missing |\n| 403 | `PROJECT_FORBIDDEN` | Actor lacks project access |\n| 404 | `PROJECT_NOT_FOUND` | Project does not exist |\n| 404 | `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` | Process does not exist in project |\n| 409 | `ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT` | Derived-view refresh cannot safely reconcile with current archive state |\n| 422 | `INVALID_ARCHIVE_REQUEST` | Cursor, limit, or derived-view refresh request is invalid |\n\n## Service Interfaces\n\n```typescript\nexport interface ArchiveFinalizationService {\n  appendFinalizedEntry(args: {\n    projectId: string;\n    processId: string;\n    entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\n    finalizationKey: string;\n    sourceObjectId?: string | null;\n    bodyText?: string | null;\n    bodyData?: { jsonText: string } | null;\n    bodyFormat: ArchiveEntry['bodyFormat'];\n    relatedArtifactVersionId?: string | null;\n    relatedSourceProvenanceId?: string | null;\n    relatedToolCallId?: string | null;\n  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry>;\n\n  appendFromProcessHistoryItem(args: {\n    projectId: string;\n    processId: string;\n    historyItem: ProcessHistoryItem;\n  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry | null>;\n}\n\nexport interface ArchiveReadService {\n  getArchive(args: {\n    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n    projectId: string;\n    processId: string;\n    cursor?: string | null;\n    limit?: number;\n  }): Promise<ArchivePage>;\n}\n\nexport interface TurnDerivationService {\n  // Rebuilds cached turns by deterministic turnId rather than recreating\n  // opaque row ids, so downstream view provenance remains stable.\n  rebuildTurns(args: { projectId: string; processId: string }): Promise<DerivedTurn[]>;\n  getTurns(args: {\n    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n    projectId: string;\n    processId: string;\n    cursor?: string | null;\n    limit?: number;\n  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\n}\n\nexport interface DerivedArchiveViewService {\n  listViews(args: {\n    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n    projectId: string;\n    processId: string;\n  }): Promise<{ views: DerivedArchiveView[] }>;\n\n  refreshViews(args: {\n    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n    projectId: string;\n    processId: string;\n  }): Promise<{ views: DerivedArchiveView[]; refreshStatus: 'settled' | 'accepted' | 'degraded' }>;\n}\n```\n\n### PlatformStore Additions\n\n```typescript\nexport interface PlatformStore {\n  appendArchiveEntry(args: {\n    projectId: string;\n    processId: string;\n    entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\n    finalizationKey: string;\n    sourceObjectId?: string | null;\n    bodyText?: string | null;\n    bodyData?: { jsonText: string } | null;\n    bodyFormat: ArchiveEntry['bodyFormat'];\n    relatedArtifactVersionId?: string | null;\n    relatedSourceProvenanceId?: string | null;\n    relatedToolCallId?: string | null;\n    entryStatus?: 'ready' | 'degraded';\n    degradationReason?: string | null;\n  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry>;\n\n  listArchiveEntries(args: {\n    processId: string;\n    cursor?: string | null;\n    limit: number;\n  }): Promise<ArchivePage>;\n\n  upsertArchiveTurns(args: {\n    projectId: string;\n    processId: string;\n    turns: DerivedTurn[];\n  }): Promise<void>;\n\n  listArchiveTurns(args: {\n    processId: string;\n    cursor?: string | null;\n    limit: number;\n  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\n\n  replaceDerivedArchiveViews(args: {\n    projectId: string;\n    processId: string;\n    views: DerivedArchiveView[];\n  }): Promise<void>;\n\n  listDerivedArchiveViews(args: {\n    processId: string;\n  }): Promise<DerivedArchiveView[]>;\n}\n```\n\nConvex function validators should mirror these shapes directly. Fastify\nservices decide finalization, derivation, and refresh policy; `PlatformStore`\nexposes only durable append/read/upsert/replace operations.\n\n## Flow-by-Flow Design\n\n### Flow 1: Capture Finalized Archive Entries\n\nThis flow covers the Story 1 primitive boundary behind AC-1.1 through AC-1.4.\nTrusted callers supply already-finalized archive-entry payloads to the durable\nappend/read primitive. Convex owns the canonical row shape, taxonomy\nvalidation, stable ordering, idempotency guard, related-id storage, and bounded\nprimitive reads.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant P as Trusted Caller\n    participant S as PlatformStore\n    participant X as Convex archiveEntries\n\n    P->>S: appendArchiveEntry(write)\n    Note over P,S: AC-1.1 finalized low-level entry payload\n    S->>X: appendArchiveEntry mutation\n    Note over S,X: AC-1.2/AC-1.3/AC-1.4 taxonomy, ordering, idempotency, related ids\n    X-->>S: ArchiveEntry\n    S-->>P: ArchiveEntry\n```\n\n### Flow 2: Keep Live State Separate from Canonical Archive\n\nThis flow covers AC-2.1 through AC-2.3. Existing WebSocket upserts continue to\nserve active UI state through `process-live-normalizer.ts` and\n`process-live.ts`. Those live messages are not archive writes. Only completed\nobjects that reach a finalization point call `ArchiveFinalizationService`,\nwhich maps finalized runtime/process objects into the Story 1 append primitive\nexactly once.\n\nRetries are safe because every finalized object supplies a `finalizationKey`.\nExamples:\n\n- accepted user response: `response:${clientRequestId}`\n- runtime model message: `model:${sourceObjectId}`\n- tool call/result pair: `tool:${relatedToolCallId}:call` and `tool:${relatedToolCallId}:result`\n- process event: `event:${sourceObjectId}`\n\n### Flow 3: Read and Reopen Archive\n\nThis flow covers AC-3.1 through AC-3.4. The user reads archive entries through\nFastify routes under the existing process path. Archive reads do not depend on\nenvironment state or live WebSocket state. `ArchiveReadService` fetches one\nbounded page from Convex, applies route validation and access rules, and\nreturns archive response rows for the client surface to render.\n\nThis flow owns displaying degraded entries already present in the response\ncontract. Deep artifact/source enrichment and lookup-failure degradation\nsemantics are added in Flow 6. Read-time degradation must not mutate the\ncanonical `archiveEntries` row unless the row itself was originally persisted\nas degraded.\n\n### Flow 4: Derive Turns\n\nThis flow covers AC-4.1 through AC-4.4. Turn derivation reads archive entries\nin ascending `sequence`, groups them deterministically, and writes cached turns\nwhen refresh/rebuild is requested.\n\nGrouping rules:\n\n1. `user_message` starts a new turn.\n2. Entries before the first user message form turn `0` if they exist.\n3. `model_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`,\n   `tool_result`, and `process_event` attach to the active turn.\n  4. A `tool_result` with `relatedToolCallId` stays in the same turn as its\n   matching `tool_call` when both are present.\n  5. Degraded related context degrades the turn, not the archive entries.\n\nRebuild behavior is explicit: Epic 7 rebuilds turns on turn/derived-view read\nor explicit derived-view refresh, not on every archive append. Rebuild upserts by\nstable `turnId` and `turnIndex`.\n\n### Flow 5: Produce Minimal Structural Views\n\nThis flow covers AC-5.1 through AC-5.5. Structural views are generated from\nturns, not from raw live state. The first slice produces:\n\n- `turn_range`: one contiguous range of turn indexes with source entry ids\n- `chunk_candidate`: a candidate grouping over one or more turns for future\n  context-management work\n\nNeither view contains model-generated summaries. `bodyText`, when present, is a\ndeterministic label or structural note such as `Turns 4-8`.\n\n### Flow 6: Connect Provenance\n\nThis flow covers AC-6.1 through AC-6.3. Archive entries store nullable related\nids. Building on the Flow 3 archive read surface, read services enrich when\npossible:\n\n- artifact context through `PlatformStore.listArtifactVersions` or a targeted\n  artifact-version read helper\n- source context through Epic 6 `sourceProvenance` reads\n- tool context through `relatedToolCallId`\n\nIf a related record is unavailable, the entry remains visible. This flow owns\nthe artifact/source lookup-failure degradation semantics: the archive entry\nstatus becomes `degraded` for the read response, or an enriched response\nincludes degraded related-context metadata without mutating the stored\ncanonical entry. Story 3 remains responsible for rendering that response\nstate to the user.\n\n### Flow 7: Return Later and Bound Long Reads\n\nThis flow covers AC-7.1 through AC-7.3. Archive entries, turns, and derived\nviews are durable or rebuildable from durable entries. Reads use cursor\npagination with default limits:\n\n- archive entries: default 100, max 200\n- turns: default 50, max 100\n- derived views: default 50\n\nA derived-view read or rebuild failure does not block archive reads. Routes\nreturn degraded view state for derived failures and keep archive entries\navailable.\n\n## Implementation Chunks\n\n| Chunk | Story | Scope | ACs | Primary Tests |\n|-------|-------|-------|-----|---------------|\n| 0 | Foundation | Contracts, Convex schema, fixtures, error codes, compatibility mapping skeletons | All support | Relevant sections: API Contracts, Data Model. Non-TC: archive contract vocabulary and finalized-only schema test |\n| 1 | Archive persistence | Append/read entries, taxonomy, ordering, idempotency, related ids | AC-1.x | Relevant sections: Flow 1, Data Model. Non-TC: atomic sequence assignment and primitive idempotency |\n| 2 | Finalization boundary | Completion hooks, live/archive separation, retry idempotency | AC-2.x | Relevant sections: Flow 2, Service Interfaces. Non-TC: live-history separation, compatibility mapping decision |\n| 3 | Archive read/reopen | Routes, access controls, empty state, bounded page contract, environment-loss reads, degraded-entry display | AC-3.x | Relevant sections: Flow 3, Route Validation. Non-TC: invalid archive request handling |\n| 4 | Turn derivation | Deterministic grouping, cached rebuild, degraded turns | AC-4.x | Relevant sections: Flow 4, Data Model. Non-TC: turn-zero grouping, rebuild stability |\n| 5 | Structural derived views | `turn_range`, `chunk_candidate`, refresh, degradation | AC-5.x | Relevant sections: Flow 5, Route Validation. Non-TC: no generated summary body, stale/rebuilt derived views |\n| 6 | Provenance coherence | Artifact/source enrichment and related-record lookup degradation semantics | AC-6.x | Relevant sections: Flow 6, API Contracts. Non-TC: none |\n| 7 | Reopen/bounded reads | Reload behavior, derived failures, long-process pagination hardening | AC-7.x | Relevant sections: Flow 7, Route Validation. Non-TC: none |\n\n## Verification\n\n| Script | Command | Use |\n|--------|---------|-----|\n| `red-verify` | `pnpm run red-verify` | After skeleton and Red tests |\n| `verify` | `pnpm run verify` | Standard development gate |\n| `green-verify` | `pnpm run green-verify` | After implementation passes tests |\n| `verify-all` | `pnpm run verify-all` | Story/Epic completion |\n\n## Deferred Items\n\n| Item | Related AC | Reason Deferred | Future Work |\n|------|------------|-----------------|-------------|\n| Historical migration/backfill from `processHistoryItems` | A7 | Epic 7 starts forward canonical archive and compatibility bridge | Later migration if needed |\n| Model-generated summaries | Scope, AC-5.x | Structural views only | Later context-management epic |\n| Model-specific prompt packing | Scope | Not required for archive truth | Later context-management epic |\n| External-source archive integration | Scope | Epic 6/7 sequence is repository-focused | Later source-integration work |\n\n## Resolved Implementation Decisions\n\n| Decision | Applied In |\n|----------|------------|\n| `relatedSourceProvenanceId` is implemented as the stable Epic 6 provenance identifier and stays string-shaped in shared contracts unless cross-table typing becomes frictionless. | Chunk 6 |\n| Turn cache rebuild happens on turn/derived-view read or explicit refresh, not on every archive append. | Chunk 4 |\n| Compatibility mapping does not publish archive entries back into the live history stream. Live history publisher remains unchanged. | Chunk 2 |\n\n## Self-Review Checklist\n\n- [x] Every Epic 7 AC has a module owner.\n- [x] Every Epic 7 Tech Design Question is answered.\n- [x] Canonical archive and live upserts stay separate.\n- [x] Turns and derived views are rebuildable, not canonical.\n- [x] Structural views exclude generated summaries.\n- [x] Verification commands use project scripts.\n","numLines":727,"startLine":1,"totalLines":727}}}
