{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":362556,"duration_api_ms":361614,"num_turns":39,"result":"I have sufficient data to produce the final output. The gate could not be executed (requires user approval), so `gateResult` is `not-run`. Code review is complete.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFinalizedEntry enforces non-null sourceObjectId for all entry kinds, stricter than the data contract (which marks it optional). All current callers (process-environment.service.ts, process-response.service.ts) supply non-null values, so no runtime breakage is present, but future callers that omit sourceObjectId will hit a throw rather than a graceful null.\",\n    \"Cache invalidation is uniformly correct across all three store implementations: archiveEntries appends invalidate archiveTurns and derivedArchiveViews; archiveTurns upserts invalidate derivedArchiveViews. This cross-story invariant is consistent in Convex, InMemoryPlatformStore, and the service layer.\",\n    \"ProcessHistoryCompatService maps only user_message, process_message, and process_event history kinds; progress_update, attention_request, and side_work_update are silently excluded (return null) and will never produce canonical archive entries. This is consistent with Assumption A7 and the compat bridge design.\",\n    \"derivedArchiveViews Convex layer uses an offset-based cursor (integer position in result set) while archiveEntries and archiveTurns use sequence/turnIndex-based cursors. Both patterns are internally consistent within their respective modules, but the asymmetry is observable at the API boundary.\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"Production route is clean: ConvexPlatformStore delegates all archive operations to real Convex mutations and queries via makeFunctionReference. No fake adapters, stubs, or fallback logic exists in the production (ConvexPlatformStore) path.\",\n    \"NullPlatformStore archive methods follow the null-object pattern (hardcoded sequence:0 on appendArchiveEntry, empty pages on list methods, no-ops on upsert/replace). NullPlatformStore is never wired into production; it is used only in non-configured test/fallback scenarios.\",\n    \"Archive services are properly wired in app.ts: DefaultArchiveReadService, DefaultTurnDerivationService, DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService are constructed with real platformStore, processAccessService, and sourceProvenanceService dependencies, decorated onto the Fastify instance, and consumed by registered archive routes.\",\n    \"derivedArchiveViews Convex service-facing mutations/queries (replaceDerivedArchiveViewsForService, listDerivedArchiveViewsForService) gate access via assertValidApiKey, adding a second access-control layer beyond Fastify auth. The internal variants are internalMutation/internalQuery and not directly callable from outside Convex.\",\n    \"Fastify owns the finalization policy boundary (ArchiveFinalizationService) as specified; Convex owns the atomic sequence assignment and idempotency guard (by_processId_and_finalizationKey index). The separation of concerns matches the tech design decision table.\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"AC-1.x: Full coverage. Convex appendArchiveEntry validates all seven entryKind literals, assigns sequence atomically, enforces idempotency via finalizationKey index, stores nullable related ids, and returns ArchiveEntry. Tests: TC-1.1a/b/c, TC-1.2a/b, TC-1.3a/b, TC-1.4a/b + primitive idempotency guard test.\",\n    \"AC-2.x: Full coverage. appendFromProcessHistoryItem gates on lifecycleState === 'finalized'; live history normalizer and process-live-normalizer remain unchanged (live/archive separation). Tests: TC-2.1a, TC-2.2a/b, TC-2.3a/b + live/archive separation test.\",\n    \"AC-3.x: Full coverage. Authenticated Fastify routes enforce project/process access via processAccessService.assertProcessAccess before reading; ArchiveReadService returns bounded pages with enriched entries and degraded-entry support; empty state returns valid empty page. Tests: TC-3.1a/b, TC-3.2a/b, TC-3.3a/b, TC-3.4a.\",\n    \"AC-4.x: Full coverage. deriveTurnsFromArchiveEntries implements all grouping rules: user_message starts a new turn, tool_result correlates via relatedToolCallId, pre-first-user-message entries form turn 0. Turns are cached as archiveTurns and rebuildable. Tests: TC-4.1a/b, TC-4.2a, TC-4.3a, TC-4.4a + turn-zero and rebuild stability tests.\",\n    \"AC-5.x: Full coverage. DerivedArchiveViewService generates turn_range views (one per turn) and chunk_candidate views (one per two turns) from cached turns. Views contain no model-generated summaries; bodyText is a deterministic structural label. Tests: TC-5.1a, TC-5.2a, TC-5.3a/b, TC-5.4a, TC-5.5a/b + no-summary-body enforcement test.\",\n    \"AC-6.x: Full coverage. enrichArchiveEntries loads artifact versions and producing-process display labels in parallel, loads source provenance entries, and propagates per-entry degradation reasons when related records are unavailable. Tests: TC-6.1a, TC-6.2a, TC-6.3a/b.\",\n    \"AC-7.x: Full coverage. Archive entries, turns, and views are durable (Convex) or rebuildable from archive entries. Services use warm-start cache patterns: empty cache + existing archive entries triggers rebuild on first read. Cursor pagination enforced at all three layers with configurable limits. Tests: TC-7.1a/b, TC-7.2a, TC-7.3a.\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"ConvexPlatformStore.appendArchiveEntry delegates to real Convex appendArchiveEntryMutation with skipQueue:true. No placeholder, no conditional bypass.\",\n    \"ConvexPlatformStore.replaceDerivedArchiveViews passes apiKey (from ConvexPlatformStore.apiKey) to replaceDerivedArchiveViewsForService, which internally calls assertValidApiKey before the real internalMutation. Real execution path.\",\n    \"NullPlatformStore.appendArchiveEntry returns a synthetic ArchiveEntry with archiveEntryId ${processId}:archive:0 and sequence:0 without writing to any store. This is the null-object pattern used in fallback/test-only contexts, not a production path. No production code path passes NullPlatformStore to archive services.\",\n    \"NullPlatformStore.listArchiveEntries, listArchiveTurns, and listDerivedArchiveViews return empty pages without reading any store. Same null-object pattern; same non-production scope.\",\n    \"The ArchiveFinalizationService integration in process-environment.service.ts (applyExecutionResultSideEffects) and process-response.service.ts (archiveAcceptedUserResponse) are real awaited calls, not fire-and-forget or silent no-ops. Failures surface to callers.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NB-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"Missing convex/archiveTurns.test.ts and convex/derivedArchiveViews.test.ts\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Test plan specifies separate Convex test files for turn upsert/list and derived-view replace/list primitives. Neither file exists. Coverage for these mutations is present in convex/archiveEntries.test.ts integration tests (which test turn derivation and view creation end-to-end), but isolated primitive tests for archiveTurns.ts and derivedArchiveViews.ts are absent.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"convex/archiveTurns.ts\", \"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-4.x\", \"AC-5.x\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NB-2\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFinalizedEntry requires non-null sourceObjectId for all entry kinds\",\n      \"evidence\": \"archive-finalization.service.ts line 31-33: if (sourceObjectId === null) { throw new Error('Finalized ${args.entryKind} entries require a sourceObjectId.'); }. The data contract (epic.md, tech-design.md) marks sourceObjectId as optional. All current callers supply non-null values, but the mismatch means any future caller that legitimately omits sourceObjectId will receive a runtime throw rather than a clean null path.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.1\", \"AC-2.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NB-3\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"findExistingEntryBySourceObjectId performs full paginated archive scan\",\n      \"evidence\": \"archive-finalization.service.ts lines 106-133: appendFromProcessHistoryItem checks for a duplicate user_message entry by scanning all archive pages in a do-while loop (limit 200 per page). This is O(n) on archive size. For processes with thousands of archive entries, this can add significant latency to user_message finalization. No index on (processId, sourceObjectId) exists in the Convex schema.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\", \"convex/schema.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-2.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NB-4\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Derived views use offset-based cursor pagination inconsistent with archive entry and turn cursors\",\n      \"evidence\": \"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts listDerivedArchiveViews: cursor is decoded as integer offset (decodedCursor); query fetches limit + decodedCursor + 1 rows and slices from offset. In contrast, archiveEntries and archiveTurns use sequence/turnIndex GT comparisons for stable cursor semantics. If derived views are replaced between page fetches, offset-based pagination can skip or repeat items.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts\", \"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-5.x\", \"AC-7.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NB-5\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"MAX_DERIVED_ARCHIVE_VIEW_LIMIT equals DEFAULT_DERIVED_ARCHIVE_VIEW_LIMIT (50); long processes approach page limit\",\n      \"evidence\": \"derived-archive-view.service.ts lines 22-23: DEFAULT_DERIVED_ARCHIVE_VIEW_LIMIT = 50, MAX_DERIVED_ARCHIVE_VIEW_LIMIT = 50. DerivedArchiveViewService generates one turn_range view per turn and one chunk_candidate per two turns. A process with 34 turns produces 34 + 17 = 51 derived views, exceeding the 50-item page limit. The first page truncates results without a next-page path being surfaced to the client sections.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-5.x\", \"AC-7.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"Epic gate (corepack pnpm run verify-all) could not be executed — command requires user approval in this session. All TC and non-TC test coverage was verified by code review only. Gate result: not-run.\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"not-run\"\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c9eda3ca-6602-4708-99a5-3d7fcbb61de5","total_cost_usd":1.6107578999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":25,"cache_creation_input_tokens":112809,"cache_read_input_tokens":2026672,"output_tokens":16317,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":112809,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4392,"cache_read_input_tokens":123582,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_toke