{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The archive route and read surfaces exist, but the main process work surface never exposes a user-facing entry point into them, so the end-to-end archive flow stops at the surface boundary instead of starting from `/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` as specified.\",\"Archive append/patch invalidation is wired through the store, but turn/view rebuild paths can still repopulate stale caches during concurrent archive patches because cache rebuild safety is checked against an incomplete archive fingerprint and is skipped entirely on cold-cache GETs.\",\"Both verification gates passed, which means current automated coverage is strong on storage/read/render happy paths but misses archive-surface discoverability and stale-cache race conditions.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Tech design called for `process-work-surface.ts` to gain archive entry points/actions, but the shared contract still exposes only the pre-Epic-7 control set and the work-surface page only handles those existing actions.\",\"Derived-view conflict handling fingerprints only `archiveEntryId`, `sequence`, and `recordedAt`, even though `patchArchiveEntry` mutates relation and degradation fields that directly affect turn derivation and derived-view status.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` passed locally.\",\"`corepack pnpm run verify-all` passed locally, including integration tests and `tests/e2e/archive-runtime-flow.spec.ts`.\",\"Coverage is good for archive persistence, read APIs, turn derivation, derived views, and provenance enrichment, but there is no client/integration coverage proving that a user can actually reach the archive surfaces from the process work surface.\",\"The shipped default execution path still does not emit low-level `archiveEntries`, so full taxonomy coverage is mostly proven through storage/service seams and injected fixtures rather than the default runtime flow.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No material test fake/stub is wired into the production boot path: `createApp` rejects `NullPlatformStore` in production and defaults to real Local/Daytona adapters plus the real Octokit checkpoint writer.\",\"The default shipped execution payload is still a high-level runtime brief that returns `archiveEntries: []` and one finalized `process_event`, so real low-level archive population depends on injected process-specific execution rather than the default runtime.\",\"Derived-view warm/refresh uses the real persistence path, but concurrent archive patches can still leave stale cached turns/views because the conflict signature ignores mutable archive fields and cold-cache GET rebuilds do not guard for conflicts at all.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-ENTRYPOINT\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Process work surface exposes no archive entry point\",\"evidence\":\"Epic 7 requires `/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` to provide entry points into archive, turn, and derived-view reads (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:469`), and the tech design explicitly says `process-work-surface.ts` should be modified for archive entry points/actions (`.../tech-design.md:162-165`). The current shared contract still only defines `start/respond/resume/rehydrate/rebuild/review/restart` actions in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:71-79,171-189`, and `apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:27-45,99-174` has no archive prop, no archive button, and no archive action handling.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-5.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-DERIVED-VIEW-CONFLICT-SIGNATURE\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Derived-view rebuild can publish stale caches after archive patches\",\"evidence\":\"`refreshViews` only compares `archiveEntryId:sequence:recordedAt` before/after rebuild (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:126-159,262-270`), but `patchArchiveEntry` can change `relatedArtifactVersionId`, `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, `relatedToolCallId`, `entryStatus`, and `degradationReason` without changing any of those fingerprint fields (`convex/archiveEntries.ts:182-226`). Those mutable fields feed turn grouping and degradation (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:210-270`). On top of that, the cold-cache GET path rebuilds and stores derived views via `warmViewsCacheOnMiss` with no conflict guard (`derived-archive-view.service.ts:53-108,173-188`). A concurrent patch can therefore repopulate turns/views from stale archive state instead of raising `ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-5.5\",\"AC-7.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-DEFAULT-RUNTIME-TAXONOMY-COVERAGE\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Default runtime still does not emit low-level canonical archive entries\",\"evidence\":\"Production boot wires the default `ScriptExecutionService` (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:285-286`), `executeFor` uses the integrated default payload (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:342-367`), and that payload hardcodes `archiveEntries: []` plus a single finalized `process_event` history item (`.../script-execution.service.ts:240-253`). The archive infrastructure accepts the full taxonomy, but the shipped default runtime only exercises compatibility-bridged history events and accepted user responses.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Whether Epic 7 intentionally stops at infrastructure-only support for low-level archive kinds in the default runtime is not stated clearly; if that is intentional, the epic/coverage docs should say so explicitly.\",\"The stale-cache finding is code-path-derived rather than reproduced under a deterministic race test; adding a concurrency-focused regression test would help lock the behavior down.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
